# Learn more https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
ios/
*.orig.*
*.jks

# `User App/android/` is deliberately NOT ignored — the native project is
# committed, because it carries hand-edits that `expo prebuild` would destroy
# (the release signingConfig, and the long-path ninja the Windows build needs).
# Its own android/.gitignore keeps build/, .gradle/ and .cxx/ out.
#
# The upload key itself must still never be committed — `*.jks` above covers
# it, and the key lives in ~/.gradle/keystores/ outside the repo.
#
# `android/gradle.properties` USED TO be excluded here, because it held the
# key's passwords in plaintext. Those have been moved to the user-level
# ~/.gradle/gradle.properties, which is where this file always said they
# belonged — so the exclusion has done its job and is gone. The file is now
# tracked, and it has to be: it carries `hermesEnabled`, `newArchEnabled` and
# `reactNativeArchitectures`, and without it a release build dies at configure
# time on `Could not get unknown property 'hermesEnabled'`. A clone that
# cannot build is what excluding it actually cost.
#
# If you ever put a password back in it, exclude it again FIRST.
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local env files
.env*.local

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
.vercel

.env

# Google Analytics / Google Cloud service-account keys — never commit these,
# wherever in the repo one ends up.
*service-account*.json
*service_account*.json
lampose-analytics*.json
